# The pre-commit installer is real source: a fresh clone has no .git/hooks, and
# per D10 the local hook is the only automated guard (no CI).
!scripts/install-git-hooks.sh
!scripts/git-hooks/

# Unity per-user editor state: machine-specific layout, search and window
# state. Unity's own template .gitignore excludes these; two engineers on
# different machines would otherwise see constant churn.
unity-project-mcp/UserSettings/
unity-visualizer/UserSettings/

# Agent scratch output: AGENTS.md already directs agents here and calls it
# gitignored, but these files were committed before that rule existed.
packages/frontend/tests/browser/out/

# HyperFrames render output: 75 MB unreferenced mp4 plus a base64 frame blob,
# both regenerable from the compositions and neither referenced by any code.
tools/hyperframes-built-this-from-a-dream/renders/

# HyperFrames waveform cache: regenerated per build, and its filenames embed a
# content hash + epoch-ms run id (e.g. v2_Built This From A Dream.mp3_7325546-1788280340000.json),
# which is unstable and meaningless to a human reader. Derived data, so it is
# regenerated rather than versioned.
tools/hyperframes-built-this-from-a-dream/.waveform-cache/

# Model-reliability advertised-layer snapshots: regenerated by
# tools/model-reliability/fetch_advertised.py, which writes one timestamped file
# per source per run. Tracking them grows the repo without bound (the README
# advises a weekly refresh = ~104 files/year) and the filenames are date+time run
# ids, which check-repo-layout rejects on principle: a run id is stale the moment
# the run is repeated and means nothing to a reader.
#
# The observed layer in the same directory (observed.jsonl) IS tracked: it is
# hand-curated session evidence, not regenerable, and it is the half that
# actually decides which model to use. Only the advertised half is derived.
tools/model-reliability/snapshots/

!tools/tests/test_doc_checkers.py
